HST Office: the Print page of the File panel ("Tệp tin" ▸ "In") has "Hủy" (Cancel) and "Quay lại" (Back) next to
its big "In" button, in Writer, Sheets, Slides and Draw.

- Both are secondary buttons of the same height as "In" (72 px), each with an icon above its label (cmd/lc_cancel,
  cmd/lc_prevrecord), a tooltip and an accessible description. Tab order: In, Hủy, Quay lại, then the copies. Access
  keys: vi "Hủ_y" (Y), "_Quay lại" (Q); en "Canc_el" (E), "_Back" (B): none of the panel's other keys (vi I_n N,
  _Số bản sao S, Thiết _lập trang L, Thêm _tùy chọn T, Calc's T_hu phóng H; en _Print, _Collate...).
- "Quay lại" closes the panel exactly as Esc and the back arrow do: the waiting print job is cancelled (its print
  settings were the job's and go with it); margins picked in the page's margins box stay (one undo step each).
- "Hủy" closes it the same way and also undoes the margins box's changes of this visit (the page's own undo steps
  "Change Page Margins" on top of the document's undo stack, sfx2 hstbackstageprintcancel.cxx), so the document is
  as it was when the page opened; it does not store the dialog's last printer/collate choice (the panel's In does).
  Printing itself runs after the panel closed (its progress dialog has its own Cancel), so there is no job being
  sent while the page is shown.
- vcl: the panel's "cancel" (hidden until now) moves into the print button's group; a new "back"; PrintDialog
  setPanelCloseHdls, PrintJobPanel::SetCloseHdls. The classic print dialog is unchanged (it has its Cancel; from
  "Thêm tùy chọn" that Cancel returns to the page).

License: sfx2/source/backstage/hstbackstageprintcancel.{hxx,cxx} are HST Office code (LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary);
the modified files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: CppunitTest_vcl_hst_print_panel testCloseButtonsBesidePrint, testCloseButtonsCallTheHost;
tests/unit/test_backstage_print_cancel_back.py; tests/runtime/check-backstage-print-cancel-back.py (Writer, Sheets:
Quay lại closes, Hủy closes and restores the margins).
